<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><img class="phero-bg" src="/assets/img/photos/paperwork.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/paperwork-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/paperwork.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="720" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">Glossary</li></ol></nav><p class="tag">Reference</p><h1>Insurance Appraisal Glossary</h1><p class="lede">43 terms you’ll meet in policies, estimates and appraisal awards, defined in plain English. Type to filter.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose"><div class="gfilter"><label for="gloss-filter">Search the glossary</label><input id="gloss-filter" type="search" placeholder="Try “coinsurance” or “umpire”" autocomplete="off"><p class="hint" data-gcount aria-live="polite">43 terms</p></div><div class="az"><a href="#g-A">A</a><a href="#g-C">C</a><a href="#g-D">D</a><a href="#g-E">E</a><a href="#g-I">I</a><a href="#g-L">L</a><a href="#g-M">M</a><a href="#g-N">N</a><a href="#g-O">O</a><a href="#g-P">P</a><a href="#g-R">R</a><a href="#g-S">S</a><a href="#g-T">T</a><a href="#g-U">U</a><a href="#g-W">W</a></div><dl class="glossary"><div class="gterm"><dt id="g-A">Actual cash value (ACV)</dt><dd>Replacement cost minus depreciation. Often the first payment on a replacement cost policy, and the full payment on an ACV policy.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Additional living expense (ALE)</dt><dd>Coverage for extra costs of living elsewhere while your home is being repaired. Also called loss of use or Coverage D.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Agreed value</dt><dd>An endorsement in which the insurer and the owner agree on a property’s value in advance, usually suspending coinsurance.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>All-risk policy</dt><dd>A policy that covers physical loss from any cause not specifically excluded. Also called open perils.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Amount of loss</dt><dd>The dollar value of the damage. This is what an appraisal panel decides.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Appraisal award</dt><dd>The written decision signed by two of the three panel members that sets the amount of loss.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Appraisal clause</dt><dd>The policy provision that lets either side demand appraisal when they disagree on the amount of loss.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Appraiser</dt><dd>The person each side names to value the loss and work with the other appraiser and the umpire.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt id="g-C">Coinsurance</dt><dd>A clause requiring you to insure property for a set percentage of its value. Falling short can reduce a claim payment.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Collateral damage</dt><dd>Damage to soft metals, screens, vents and other items that helps show hail size, direction and date.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Cosmetic damage exclusion</dt><dd>An endorsement, common on metal roofs, that excludes dents or marks that do not affect function.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Coverage A</dt><dd>Dwelling coverage for the house itself and attached structures.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Coverage B</dt><dd>Other structures coverage for detached garages, sheds, fences and similar buildings.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Coverage C</dt><dd>Personal property coverage for contents.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt id="g-D">Declarations page</dt><dd>The summary page of your policy listing limits, deductibles, endorsements and the policy period.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Deductible</dt><dd>The portion of a covered loss you pay before the policy pays.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Depreciation</dt><dd>A reduction in value for age, wear and obsolescence.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Derecho</dt><dd>A long-lived, widespread windstorm produced by a line of thunderstorms. Eastern South Dakota was hit by one on May 12, 2022.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Disinterested</dt><dd>Having no financial or personal stake in the outcome. Many appraisal clauses require appraisers to be disinterested or independent.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt id="g-E">Endorsement</dt><dd>A written change to a policy that adds, removes or modifies coverage.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Estimate</dt><dd>An itemized list of repairs with quantities and prices. Appraisal panels work from line-item estimates.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt id="g-I">Ice dam</dt><dd>A ridge of ice at the roof edge that traps meltwater, which can then back up under shingles and into the house.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Ingress</dt><dd>Water or debris entering a building through an opening, such as one created by wind or hail.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt id="g-L">Line item</dt><dd>A single entry in an estimate for one task or material, with a quantity and unit price.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt id="g-M">Matching</dt><dd>The question of whether repairs must reasonably match undamaged areas in color, texture and appearance.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Mitigation</dt><dd>Reasonable steps to prevent further damage after a loss, such as tarping a roof or drying a basement.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt id="g-N">Named peril</dt><dd>A policy that covers only the causes of loss listed in it, common for some farm buildings.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt id="g-O">Ordinance or law coverage</dt><dd>Coverage for extra costs to meet current building codes during repair or rebuilding.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Overhead and profit (O&amp;P)</dt><dd>A contractor’s general costs and margin, often 10% and 10%, added when a project requires coordination of several trades.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt id="g-P">Pitch</dt><dd>The steepness of a roof, written as rise over 12 inches of run, such as 7/12.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Proof of loss</dt><dd>A sworn statement of the amount claimed, which carriers may request within a set time.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt id="g-R">Recoverable depreciation</dt><dd>Depreciation withheld from the first payment that you can recover after repairs are completed.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Replacement cost value (RCV)</dt><dd>The cost to repair or replace damaged property with materials of like kind and quality, without deducting depreciation.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Reservation of rights</dt><dd>A letter in which the insurer says it is handling a claim while reserving the right to deny coverage later.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt id="g-S">Scope</dt><dd>The list of damaged items and the work needed to repair them.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Square</dt><dd>A roofing unit equal to 100 square feet of roof surface.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Sub-limit</dt><dd>A lower limit within a policy for a specific type of loss, such as mold, trees or sewer backup.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Supplement</dt><dd>A request to add items or increase amounts in the carrier’s estimate, supported by documentation.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Surplus lines</dt><dd>Insurance written by carriers not licensed as standard insurers in the state, often used for hard-to-place risks.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Suit limitation</dt><dd>The policy clause setting how long you have to file a lawsuit against the insurer.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt id="g-T">Test square</dt><dd>A marked area of roof, often 10 feet by 10 feet, where hail hits are counted.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt id="g-U">Umpire</dt><dd>The neutral third member of an appraisal panel who decides items the two appraisers cannot agree on.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt id="g-W">Wind and hail deductible</dt><dd>A separate deductible for windstorm or hail losses, often a percentage of the dwelling limit.</dd></div></dl></article>
<aside class="aside"><div class="box box-call"><h2 class="box-t">Talk it through first</h2><p>The first conversation is free. We’ll tell you plainly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="big-tel" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn ink" href="/get-a-claim-review/">Send claim details</a></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-t">Resources</h2><ul class="box-list"><li><a href="/inside-the-appraisal-process/">Inside the appraisal process</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-questions-answered/">Appraisal questions answered</a></li><li><a href="/insurance-appraisal-glossary/" aria-current="page">Appraisal glossary</a></li><li><a href="/storm-claim-articles/">Storm claim articles</a></li></ul></div></aside></div>
